# Shell scripts must keep LF endings so they execute on Linux hosts after
# checkout/scp from Windows. With core.autocrlf=true a CRLF working-tree copy
# gets scp'd to the VPS, where bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r` and aborts with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name". eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
